        "question": {
          ":question/id": "96c0f36b-1fdb-532f-a6b6-6e7c5fa3df33",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
          ":question/problem": "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -9 & 9 & -9 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -9 & 9 & -9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PO$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $OR$ is well defined",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $O$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, $P$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix, and $R$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $O$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $P$ and $5$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $O$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{5\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.",
