          ":question/id": "8bf00f74-b8b0-5cce-80be-661ed70e2a73",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "$$\nO=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -9 & 9 & -9 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -9 & 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $PO$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $OR$ is well defined",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $O$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $P$ is a $4\\times 1$ column vector, and $R$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $5$ columns in $O$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times 5}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{4\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there is $1$ column in $P$ and $1$ row in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{O}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 5}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $O$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false.",
